# Build output. The binary is compiled from source and never committed: a
# tracked binary is rewritten by every build, so a clean worktree turns dirty
# on a command that changed no source at all, and the diff is megabytes of
# noise that hides the change the commit is actually about.
/arxi-tui
/arxi-tui.exe
# The whole bin/ tree is build output, so ignore the directory rather than
# enumerating each artifact. Enumerating them is what let bin/arxi-tui.exe~ — an
# editor/build backup the exact-path patterns did not match — get committed as a
# 4.9 MB tracked binary, the precise failure this comment warns about.
/bin/
